### Discovering character-specific Effect records

Effect records are character-content dependent. A character can gain Effects from spells, features, items, or other content, so this reference cannot enumerate every possible Effect name.

Effect **instances** are dynamic, while the reusable record schema is documented below. `_enabled` controls whether the record participates in the canonical model; `_active` stores current Effect state. Enabled Effects can persist with `_active:false`. Both values are mapped for reads, but Effect creation, removal, and active-state writes are not documented as universal ScriptCards lifecycle operations.

Use the `effects` typed collection to discover the actual Effect records on the selected character:

```scard
!script {{
  --#beaconsheet|1
  --#sourcetoken|[@SC_SelectedTokens(0)]
  --#title|Beacon Effect Probe
  --#leftsub|[*S:character_name]

  --%EffectIndex|0;99;1
    --&EffectName|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->name]
    --?"[&EffectName]" -eq "undefined"|%!

    --+|[b]Effect [&EffectIndex]: [&EffectName][/b]
    --+_id|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->_id]
    --+type|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->type]
    --+name|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->name]
    --+recordName|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->recordName]
    --+shortID|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->shortID]
    --+_enabled|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->_enabled]
    --+_active|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->_active]
    --+description|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->description]
    --+category|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->category]
    --+damageType|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->damageType]
    --+label|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->label]
    --+source|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->source]
    --+compendiumPageID|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->compendiumPageID]
    --+createdTime|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->createdTime]
    --+parentID|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->parentID]
    --+childIDs|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->childIDs]
  --%|
}}
```

The numeric index is for discovery only. For reusable reads, prefer a unique Effect `name` or `shortID`, for example:

```scard
[*S:effects->[&EffectShortID]->description]
[*S:effects->[&EffectShortID]->parentID]
```

#### Generic Effect fields

`[effect]` is a documentation placeholder; replace it with a unique Effect name, `shortID`, or numeric discovery index.

| Field | Generic ScriptCards location | Values / domain | Meaning / write guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
